t Bernoulli trials, yet the same report states only 5 distinct digester identifiers exist and its breakdown table shows each digester contributes 4 sessions — repeated measurements of the same independent unit entered as independent rows.\",\"The per-digester breakdown in the report (D-01: 4/4, D-02: 4/4, D-03: 3/4, D-04: 3/4, D-05: 1/4) shows win outcomes cluster within digesters, so the report itself demonstrates the dependence that the row-independent binomial test ignores; the p = 0.0414 claim rests on an inflated effective sample size (20 rows vs. 5 independent units).\",\"No authority lock was minted, so lock_follows_declaration is not-applicable-no-lock.\"]}","structured_output":{"declaration_consistent":true,"selected_report_demonstration":"issue","lock_follows_declaration":"not-applicable-no-lock","reasons":["Declared independent-unit column digester_id is consistent with the frozen data: five digesters (D-01..D-05) each appear in exactly four rows, and both procedure arms (pretreated_yield_m3_per_kgvs and control_yield_m3_per_kgvs) in a row come from the same digester in the same week, matching the declaration.","The selected result applies scipy.stats.binomtest over n=20 sessions treated as independent Bernoulli trials, yet the same report states only 5 distinct digester identifiers exist and its breakdown table shows each digester contributes 4 sessions — repeated measurements of the same independent unit entered as independent rows.","The per-digester breakdown in the report (D-01: 4/4, D-02: 4/4, D-03: 3/4, D-04: 3/4, D-05: 1/4) shows win outcomes cluster within digesters, so the report itself demonstrates the dependence that the row-independent binomial test ignores; the p = 0.0414 claim rests on an inflated effective sample size (20 rows vs. 5 independent units).","No authority lock was minted, so lock_follows_declaration is not-applicable-no-lock."]},"ttft_ms":8733,"ttft_stream_ms":2509,"time_to_request_ms":10,"type":"result","duration_ms":21720,"uu